{
 "title": "Replication Spec - Price Responses of Rwandan Tungsten Exports under Conflict Minerals Regulation",
 "hypothesis": "Export demand price elasticity for Rwandan tungsten (HS 261100) varies across institutional periods defined by Dodd-Frank implementation and destination composition, estimated by exchange-rate pass-through when unit values are missing.",
 "data_sources": [
  "UN Comtrade importer-reported for Rwanda HS 261100 monthly",
  "UN Comtrade global importer-reported for HS 261100 for world price",
  "FXTOP monthly exchange rates"
 ],
 "sample": "Monthly importer-reported mirror trade panel for Rwandan tungsten ores and concentrates HS 261100. Export value X_jt observed; export quantity Q_jt missing for some importer-months. Importer j is reporting importer. World price P^W_t constructed from global HS 261100 importer reports. Exchange rate E_jt = importer currency per Rwandan franc from FXTOP. Product filter: HS 261100 only. Reporter filter: importer-reported. Exporter filter: Rwanda.",
 "period_start": "January 2009",
 "period_end": "December 2023",
 "method": [
  "1. Construct world average price for month t: P^W_t = sum_i V_it / sum_i Q_it where V_it, Q_it are import value and quantity of HS 261100 reported by importer i in UN Comtrade global file. Use to capture common world market price.",
  "2. Merge importer-reported Rwandan export value X_jt with ln E_jt (FXTOP monthly) and ln P^W_t by month t.",
  "3. Assume Rwanda is small price taker. Demand: ln Q_jt = alpha_j + eta ln P^{imp}_jt + u_jt. Import price: ln P^{imp}_jt = ln E_jt + ln P^{exp}_jt + tau_j. Export price response: ln P^{exp}_jt = delta_j + omega ln X_jt + lambda ln P^{W}_t + v_jt.",
  "4. Substitute to reduced form: ln X_jt = mu_j + beta ln E_jt + gamma ln P^{W}_t + epsilon_jt where mu_j is importer fixed effect. Relationship beta = (1+eta)/(1-omega(1+eta)) => eta = beta/(1+beta*omega) -1.",
  "5. Separately estimate inverse-supply omega via ln UV_jt = a_j + omega ln X_jt + lambda ln P^{W}_t + e_jt where UV_jt = X_jt/Q_jt on subsample with Q_jt available; cluster SE at importer. Result omega 0.04384 SE 0.02660 95% CI [-0.00829, 0.09597] not significant at 5%. Approximate omega=0.",
  "6. Under omega=0, eta = beta -1. Estimate per period by importer fixed-effects OLS with cluster at importer level: ln X_jt on ln E_jt and ln P^{W}_t. Report beta, SE, gamma, SE, implied eta = beta-1, 95% CI for eta from beta SE. Do separately for Period 1 Jan.2009--Dec.2012, Period 2 Jan.2013--Apr.2017, Period 3 May 2017--May 2019, Period 4 Jun.2019--Dec.2023. Period boundaries based on SEC rule Aug 2012 effective 2013, SEC enforcement change Apr 2017, destination composition shift Jun 2019.",
  "7. Coefficient-difference test for periods r vs s: pool r and s, estimate FE model with importer x period FE, period-specific beta and gamma, cluster by importer. H0: beta_r = beta_s. Delta = beta_s - beta_r, SE(Delta)=sqrt(Var(beta_s)+Var(beta_r)-2Cov), t=Delta/SE. Under omega~0, beta diff = eta diff. Report difference, SE, t, p."
 ],
